{"id": "nl0.json", "pointer": "/inferences/1", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "R002", "inputs": [], "output": "N002", "definitions": ["D013", "D014"], "locals": [{"symbol": "tau", "type": "positive real", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix any tau>0.", "scope": "argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S002", "objects": [], "from_inputs": [], "from_local": []}, {"symbol": "alpha", "type": "real", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix alpha in R.", "scope": "argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S002", "objects": [], "from_inputs": [], "from_local": []}, {"symbol": "beta", "type": "real", "kind": "arbitrary", "declaration": "Fix beta in R.", "scope": "argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S002", "objects": [], "from_inputs": [], "from_local": []}, {"symbol": "h", "type": "smooth complex function on [0,tau]", "kind": "definition", "declaration": "h(s)=exp(-i*alpha*s)-Mavg_tau(exp(-i*alpha*.)).", "scope": "argument", "start": "S001", "end": "S002", "objects": ["tau", "alpha", "Mavg"], "from_inputs": [], "from_local": []}], "argument": [{"id": "S001", "text": "Fix tau>0, alpha,beta real. If either phase vanishes its exponential is 1 and the covariance is zero. In the remaining case assume L1: alpha*beta!=0. Define h(s)=exp(-i*alpha*s)-Mavg_tau(exp(-i*alpha*.)). Then eta=tau^(-1)integral_0^tau h(s)exp(-i*beta*s)ds. The elementary integral estimate |exp(-i*alpha*s)-exp(-i*alpha*r)|<=|alpha||s-r| gives |h(s)|<=tau^(-1)integral_0^tau |alpha||s-r|dr<=tau|alpha|. Consequently |eta|<=tau|alpha|. At s=0,tau the sharper integrals are each tau|alpha|/2, so |h(0)|+|h(tau)|<=tau|alpha|; also integral_0^tau|h'(s)|ds=tau|alpha|.", "uses": [], "uses_local": [], "objects": ["tau", "alpha", "beta", "h", "eta", "Mavg"], "produces": [{"id": "F001", "statement": "Under L1, |eta_tau(alpha,beta)|<=tau|alpha| and |h(0)|+|h(tau)|+integral_0^tau|h'|<=2*tau|alpha|.", "objects": ["tau", "alpha", "beta", "h", "eta"], "assumptions": ["L1"], "binders": []}], "introduces": ["L1"], "discharges": []}, {"id": "S002", "text": "Integration by parts against exp(-i*beta*s), which has nonzero derivative factor -i*beta under L1, gives |eta|<= (|h(0)|+|h(tau)|+integral|h'|)/(tau|beta|)<=2|alpha/beta| by F001. The defining covariance is symmetric in alpha,beta; repeating both estimates with the phases interchanged gives |eta|<=tau|beta| and |eta|<=2|beta/alpha|. Take their minima, discharge L1, and include the zero-phase case already calculated. Universal introduction proves the output assertion.", "uses": [], "uses_local": ["F001"], "objects": ["tau", "alpha", "beta", "h", "eta"], "produces": [], "introduces": [], "discharges": ["L1"]}], "applications": [], "rules": ["direct", "forall_introduction", "implication_introduction"]}, "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}
